3) Having heard learned counsel for the parties and perused the material on record, the following question arise for consideration in this case:
1. Whether the writ petition seeking relief in the nature of compensation for electrocution, which involves determination of disputed questions of fact, is maintainable under Article 226 of the Constitution of India;
2.

Whether in the given facts and circumstances, the respondents can be held negligent in maintaining the electric wires so as to fasten liability upon them to compensate Next of Kin of the deceased;
3. To what amount the petitioners can be held entitled to in the light of pleadings and the documentary evidence on record;
4) Indisputably, the cause of death of the deceased is shock due to electrocution.

